      "content": "1. MEANING OF FISCAL POLICY"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Fiscal policy outlines the objectives, budget components, and management of public debt.",
        "The Fiscal Responsibility and Budget Management (FRBM) Act (2003) provides targets and year-wise evolution for fiscal discipline.",
        "Taxation in India is divided into Direct and Indirect Taxes, with a structured GST system.",
        "Analyzing deficit types and comparisons is essential for understanding public expenditure and economic stability."
      ],
